    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="1309" n="1151" xml:id="pg1151"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 80.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 121, of the 12th instant, on the subject of Mr. Henry Love Clarke’s
                    desire to have certain definite information regarding the measures taken by the
                    Mexican authorities against the marauding Yaqui Indians in the State of Sonora,
                    during certain specified intervals, with relation to the murders of the
                    MacKensie party and Mr. Albert W. Sayles.</p>
                <p>The department concurs in your view of the case, and thinks that it will be
                    inadvisable to take the matter up at this time with the Mexican Government.</p>
                <p>Copies of your dispatch No. 80 and of Consul Hostetter’s letter of February 3,
                    1906, to the governor of Sonora, together with a copy of your No. 121, have been
                    furnished to Mr. Clarke.</p>
                <p>At the time of transmitting to you Mr. Clarke’s letter of May 24, the department
                    had not received your full and satisfactory dispatch No. 80, which makes any
                    further inquiry of the Mexican Government at present seem inexpedient.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
